// CROWN — one HOF parameter reaches a `!E` frame by two paths, one masked
// by an install that absorbs E and one direct. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 14 through the pinned boot (measured
// 2026-09-23). The bound the parameter carries is the MEET of what each
// path allows: through the install E is admitted, directly it is not.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler absorb { op() => resume(5) }
fn g(f) with !E = (f(1) ~> absorb) + f(1)
fn caller() = g({ x => op() + x })
handler eh { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = (caller()) ~> eh
